{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The fee rests on a driver-pressed 'arrived' marker at 18:44:30, and that marker is not backed by the trace. POL-NS-01(b) requires the gps_trace to place the driver inside the pickup geofence 'at or before the timestamp of that event'; on the exported trace the first fix inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius is at 18:44:45, fifteen seconds AFTER the tap, and there is no earlier in-radius fix from which the clock could run. The policy deliberately runs the waiting clock from GPS entry into the geofence and not from the driver tapping 'arrived'. POL-NS-05 only recomputes the clock where the marker is found FALSE - more than 300 m from the pin, or at 15 km/h or more - and the exported trace establishes neither threshold at 18:44:30; nor does POL-NS-12 rescue the marker, because trip_record.platform_policy.arrival_marker is BUTTON (a driver-pressed marker), not GPS_AUTO, so the platform's full-resolution arrival measurement is not in play. The platform, which asserts the fee, carries the burden on each limb of the conjunctive POL-NS-01, and limb (b) is not made out.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00214", "EV-GPS-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-12"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.runs[0].first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver never held position for the free waiting period in force. On his own trace the longest unbroken hold inside the arrival radius is 185 seconds (18:49:35 to 18:52:40) and the earlier hold is only 170 seconds (18:44:45 to 18:47:35); the free waiting period for this trip is 300 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec). POL-NS-01(c) requires the driver to have 'held position inside that geofence for a continuous dwell of at least' that period, and the trace shows precisely what the rider describes - the car at the bay, then away, then back, then cancelling. The rider's account that he 'never even stayed 5 minutes in one place' is corroborated to the second. The driver's answer will be POL-NS-06(i), which lets separate in-geofence intervals be summed where a kerb restriction (here the KERB_RESTRICTION advisory EV-ADVIS-00214-01) made holding position unlawful; but limb (i) is drafted as a qualification on the POL-NS-06 refund arithmetic - it presupposes the circling driver whose time 'should count' in that computation - and it cannot manufacture the continuous dwell that POL-NS-01(c) makes a condition of the charge itself.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00214", "EV-TRIP-00214", "EV-ADVIS-00214-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing turns on where the rider's own device was. POL-NS-06 makes the waiting-period test strict and directs that the fee be refunded 'whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages'. The trace records no qualifying rider fix inside the 150 m rider-presence radius (rider_qualifying_fix_count 0), but rider presence is not a limb of POL-NS-01 and cannot convert a dwelling shortfall into a chargeable no-show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own account confirms the gap the rider complains of. He posted at 18:45:10 that he was 'at the ION PHV bay along Orchard Turn'; the rider answered at 18:46:20 that she was 'coming down now'; and the trace puts his departure from the arrival radius at 18:47:35 - two minutes after his own locating message and 75 seconds after hers. For the whole of 18:47:35 to 18:49:35 the bay was empty while the rider was on her way down, and the total in-radius time the driver can point to is 355 seconds, under six minutes and by no measure the continuous period the charge requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00214", "EV-CHAT-00214"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.runs[1].first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
